  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p><strong>Awarded For:</strong> An act of extreme piety, one that proves unmistakably you are a fervent and loyal follower of your deity in the eyes your god and their servants. Recovering long lost religious artifacts, successfully launching a crusade against enemies of a given deity or going on a years-long spiritual journey across the Old World, aiding as many temples as possible enough for word to reach the Arch Lectures of the various faiths.</p><p><strong>Description:</strong> A gold medallion, inlaid with iron and the image of a hammer etched in, with a silver skull in the hammer’s head.</p><p><strong>Bonuses:</strong> +10 to @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.9xR9uO8FIvi4YsJp]{Pray} Tests and the @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.wNvPXAhlKABl6hpk]{Pure Soul} Talent is added to the Talent list of any career you are in.</p><h3>Medal Notes</h3>\n<p>Talents granted by medals apply only to the <strong>original recipient</strong>. Non-talent bonuses require the medal to be <strong>worn</strong> by the earner. Non-earners do not gain these benefits — the GM enforces recipient rules (no automatic earner lock). Medals can be identified with Easy (+40) Lore (Empire / Heraldry / History). Fake medals: Evaluate + Numismatics (GM difficulty).</p>"
    },
